<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <OutputType>Library</OutputType>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    What a test of an Avalonia control needs, shared by the test projects that
    have one: the headless platform with Skia under it, the font the program
    ships, and a base class that opens windows and settles layout. Skia is what
    lets a test see pixels rather than throw: the default headless drawing
    backend does no rasterizing, and a test that cannot see what it drew passed
    while the number boxes in the step list rendered empty.

    No test lives here, so it takes the extensibility package and not xunit.v3,
    which makes a project one the test runner is pointed at.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.v3.extensibility.core" />
    <PackageReference Include="Avalonia.Headless" />
    <PackageReference Include="Avalonia.Skia" />
    <PackageReference Include="Avalonia.Fonts.Inter" />
    <PackageReference Include="Avalonia.Themes.Fluent" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Headless/ is Avalonia.Headless.XUnit's own source (MIT, from
    src/Headless/Avalonia.Headless.XUnit in AvaloniaUI/Avalonia), compiled here
    instead of referenced as a package. The shipped assembly is built against
    xunit.v3 3.2.2 and its discoverer throws MissingMethodException on 4.x,
    which loses every UI test at discovery; built from source it is compiled
    against whatever xunit the project uses.

    Kept as close to upstream as it can be, so a newer Avalonia can be diffed
    against it: what changed is the xunit 4 extensibility API it sits on — the
    scheduling values ISelfExecutingXunitTestCase.Run now carries, threaded down
    to the runner contexts, and a discoverer override whose signature moved. The
    four AvaloniaTestFramework* files are left out, being the assembly-attribute
    route that [AvaloniaFact] does not take.

    Delete the folder and reference the package again once Avalonia ships one
    built against xunit.v3 4.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Update="Headless\*.cs" Visible="true" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
